@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title `proveo clean` — reclaim leaked run state without killing live runs

actor "Maintainer" as MT

node "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "cmd/proveo clean\ngathers inventory · executes plan" as CMD <<app>>
  component "internal/clean\nBuildPlan(inv, opts) — pure" as CORE <<app>>

  frame "Inventory" as INV <<host>> {
    component "egress session containers\n(mitm · squid · ollama)" as C <<app>>
    component "leaked DinD sidecars\n(not session-labeled)" as D <<app>>
    component "egress networks\n+ HasEndpoints" as N <<app>>
    database "<stateDir>/egress/<sid>\nholds injected broker.env" as ST <<error>>
    database "proveo/* images" as IMG <<db>>
    database "PROVEO_HOME (~/.proveo)\nsessions + seeded config" as PH <<db>>
  }
}

MT ARROW_MAIN CMD
CMD ARROW_MAIN CORE : Inventory + Options
CORE ARROW_MAIN CMD : Plan{remove…, SkippedLive}

CORE ARROW_MAIN C : routine — dead sessions only
CORE ARROW_MAIN D : routine
CORE ARROW_MAIN N : routine — only when no endpoints
CORE ARROW_ERROR ST : routine — successLabel(wipes broker.env)
CORE ARROW_OPTIONAL IMG : ""--deep"" only
CORE ARROW_OPTIONAL PH : ""--homes"" only

note right of CORE
  **Pure decision core.** ""BuildPlan"" performs no I/O:
  ""cmd/proveo"" gathers the inventory and executes. That
  is what makes the liveness rules unit-testable without
  Docker.

  **Liveness is the invariant.** A running container, or
  a network that still has endpoints, is left alone and
  reported in ""SkippedLive"" — a concurrent ""proveo run""
  must survive a clean. ""--force"" is the only override.
end note

note bottom of ST
  Wiping egress state is a **security** action, not just
  disk hygiene: a crashed run can leave the injected
  ""broker.env"" (the real provider key) on disk. Routine
  clean removes it.
end note

note bottom of PH
  Deliberately excluded from both routine and ""--deep"":
  it is the user's durable session history, not run
  ephemera. Upstream sidecar bases (squid, ollama,
  docker:dind) are likewise left — shared and cheap to
  re-pull. See _spec/internal/proveohome/proveo-home-components.puml
end note
@enduml
